# Species-side coset-orbit data and kernel-cheap checkers (species-side coset orbits, part C)

The COLUMN/species mirror of `Twin2/NormOrbitData.lean` (the normalizer-orbit
partition). For each of the 148
subgroup-class representatives `H = reps r`, with certified derived subgroup
`H' = hpData r` and certified coset transversal `T = transData r` of `H'` in `H`
(both discharged in `Twin2/SpeciesCosets.lean`/`Twin2/SpeciesLink.lean`), the compiled emitter
`Twin2/SpeciesEmit.lean` produces, as untrusted data re-checked here by kernel `decide`:

* `cosetActData r` — one index table per generator of `N_G(H)` (the certified
  `normGens r`): `cosetActData[r][k][p]` is the transversal index of the
  `H'`-coset of `nₖ⁻¹ · T[p] · nₖ` (orientation matching `normMats_realize`);
* `cosetLabel r` — the orbit label (least-index representative) of each coset;
* `cosetIsRep r` / `cosetTreeGen r` / `cosetTreePar r` / `cosetTreeDepth r` — the
  BFS spanning-tree witnesses connecting each coset to its orbit representative.

The checkers are: for `cosetActOK` a single `siftB` per `(r,k,p)` — the fact
`(T[tab])⁻¹ · (nₖ⁻¹ · T[p] · nₖ) ∈ H'`, i.e. the emitted table entry is the
genuine coset of the conjugate — plus label-invariance; for `cosetTreeOK` pure
`Nat` bookkeeping. `Twin2/SpeciesOrbits.lean` assembles the whole-range checks and the
aggregate counts (`2724` orbits; fibre `{1:148, 5:2376, 25:200}`).

**Scope note.** This layer certifies the `N_G(H)`-orbit partition of the coset
transversals. That `normGens r` genuinely generate `N_G(H)` is
`normGens_generate` (`LeanDring/P5/Certificate/ConjugacyClasses/Twin2/NormLink.lean`); that `T` is a genuine transversal of the
genuine derived subgroup is `Twin2/SpeciesLink.lean`. The per-step realization (table entry
= conjugate coset) is `cosetActOK` here.
